ARTICLE 28.- The medical care of indigent disabled persons consists of the reduction or 
exemption of fees, in proportion to their Permanent Potential Incapacity (PPI) rate for: 
- Consultation; 
- laboratory examinations; 
- radiography or medical imaging; 
-  hospitalization; 
-  medical evacuation; 
- purchase of certain medicines, in specialized institutions and public or privat e 
health facilities,  


